pack.sh is staged into this directory by ../../prepare-context.sh. It is the
FreeBSD installer's server-files profile (files/packs/tmp4-r40250.pack), copied
in verbatim -- not edited, not a reimplementation.

The client builder uses two functions out of it:

    pack_prepare_client()   unpack the client, drop what players must not get,
                            add the start-here readme, repack
    pack_apply_ip()         and, through it, p_write_serverinfo(), which knows
                            where this client actually reads its server list
                            from and which names that file has to define

That is the same arrangement the game image uses for pack_apply_rates(): one
copy of the knowledge, so the FreeBSD server and the Docker server cannot drift
apart about what a correct client looks like.

The file is deliberately not committed -- it belongs to files/packs/ and having
a second copy in git is exactly the drift this design avoids. Check that the
image is carrying the file you think it is:

    docker compose run --rm client-builder status | grep profile
    md5sum ../../../files/packs/tmp4-r40250.pack
